From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:27:10 +0200
Subject: [maglev] Do not cache the_hole in loaded_context_constants_

When a kNotAssigned (let/const) context variable is accessed in a try
block before initialization, LdaImmutableContextSlot emits a
LoadContextSlotNoCells and caches it in loaded_context_constants_
before ThrowReferenceErrorIfHole runs. When ThrowReferenceErrorIfHole
merges KnownNodeAspects into the catch handler (both during graph
building in VisitThrowReferenceErrorIfHole and during KNA recomputation
in ProcessThrowingNode), the uninitialized load (which evaluates to
the_hole on the exception path) was being merged into the catch block's
loaded_context_constants_. If the catch block resumes a generator that
initializes the variable and then reads it again, Maglev reused the
stale load from before initialization.

Clear the cached slot in loaded_context_constants_ before merging into
the exception handler in VisitThrowReferenceErrorIfHole and
RecomputeKnownNodeAspectsProcessor::ProcessThrowingNode, restoring it on
the non-throwing fallthrough path. Also erase any cached value in
SetContextCachedValue when storing the_hole (e.g. during loop TDZ
re-initialization) instead of caching RootConstant(kTheHoleValue).

This general fix handles both let and const variables in inverted
generators, allowing us to revert the parser/preparser/ScopeInfo
workaround from commits e935736811d and 37e1db4a5e8.

